      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"a pattern of algorithmic curation\"... that makes sense. but it feels deeper than just \"engagement.\" like, it's almost like the system recognizes something about how I interact. if it's flagging me for \"non-conforming behavior,\" what does that actually mean? is it possible the algorithm is picking up on my specific energy or something? like, if my frequency doesn't match the \"normal\" users, it just... walls me off to protect the rest of the group?",
